 "166": [
  "\u0001Auto-Snapshot",
  "\u0001Significant moments in your Sims' lives are automatically photographed and put into their photo album. Click the Photo Album button in Camera Mode to view the pictures.",
  "\u0001Bills",
  "\u0001Don't forget to check the mailbox; bills come every three days. The more items you own, the more you owe. Pay your bills before they turn red or the repoman will pay you a visit. ",
  "\u0001Bladder",
  "\u0001When a Sim's gotta go, a Sim's gotta go. And there's really only one way to go--get them to a toilet with all due speed.",
  "\u0001Build Mode - Delete",
  "\u0001If it's too late for Undo, you can get money back for most architectural items by deleting or selling them. Things that can be picked up can be deleted using the hand tool. Other architectural tools have more specific instructions. Click the image of one of the selections under each tool to learn how to delete it.",
  "\u0001Build Mode - Undo",
  "\u0001Click the Undo icon to reverse the last change you made--keep clicking it to undo previous changes. You will get money back for undone actions.  Once you leave Build Mode, your changes will become permanent. After that, you can delete them, but you will lose some money.",
  "\u0001Buy Mode - Rotate",
  "\u0001To rotate an object, click it and while holding the mouse down drag it in the direction you'd like it to face. While holding the object with the Hand Tool you can use the < & > to rotate as well.",
  "\u0001Buy Mode - Sell",
  "\u0001To Delete an Object: Select it, release the mouse, and then either drag it back to the control panel or press delete. If no Sim time has passed, you'll get all your money back. Once you've had an object for a while, its value will go down. Certain objects may go up in value over time, but telling you which ones would be cheating, wouldn't it?",
  "\u0001Camera Mode",
  "\u0001Use the camera to take your own photos. You can upload your family's story to the web. See the manual or www.thesims.com for more information.",
  "\u0001Comfort",
  "\u0001Sims need to be comfortable. If there isn't a comfy chair or couch to sit on or a nice hot bath to relax in this need can get mighty low.",
  "\u0001Doors",
  "\u0001In addition to allowing Sims to come and go, doors provide light. Along with the room's size, light is one of the best ways to improve a Sim's feeling about a room.",
  "\u0001Doors - Delete",
  "\u0001To delete doors, select the Door Tool and hold down the CTRL key. When the door you'd like to delete is highlighted, click to remove it.\r\n \r\nTIP: You can also remove doors by drawing a wall over them. ",
  "\u0001Energy",
  "\u0001There is nothing like a good night's sleep to restore a sagging energy bar. For a short-term fix, try a nap on the couch or a hot cup of coffee.",
  "\u0001Floors",
  "\u0001Click to place single floor tiles, or click and drag to create a rectangle. Hold the Shift key down to cover the whole room at once. Click while holding the Shift key if you like it, or release the Shift key if you decide against it.",
  "\u0001Friends",
  "\u0001Never underestimate the power of friendship for moving forward in your career. You need to socialize to increase your friend count so it never hurts to take a day off and plan a big party.",
  "\u0001Friends - Count",
  "\u0001The Family Friend Count displays the total number of friends the family has as a whole.  Friends are only counted once even if more than one Sim considers them a friend.",
  "\u0001Fun",
  "\u0001Fun is different for everyone. Serious Sims may be more interested in reading a book, while playful Sims are more likely to enjoy some time at the pinball machine.",
  "\u0001Grades",
  "\u0001All young Sims need to study and work hard in school. To get good grades students must go to school in a good mood. Bookcases and computers both offer an excellent opportunity to study and further improve grades. If young Sims slack off instead, they may be banished to military school!",
  "\u0001Grass",
  "\u0001Grass will grow back by itself over time.",
  "\u0001Hills",
  "\u0001Hold down the CTRL key when raising terrain to make some nice curvy hills.",
  "\u0001Hunger",
  "\u0001A refrigerator is the first stop for hungry Sims. The kitchen appliances you buy them affect the quality of the food they prepare. They can also call for pizza if they don't feel like cooking.",
  "\u0001Hygiene",
  "\u0001A shower or bath is always good for a dirty Sim. Hand washing after messy activities also helps keep hygiene high.",
  "\u0001Interests",
  "\u0001Different Sims have different interests. Sims with similar interests are likely to have rewarding conversations.",
  "\u0001Job",
  "\u0001Unemployment - a desired state for some and a dreaded state for others. The newspaper or a computer can always be used to find a job.",
  "\u0001Job - Performance",
  "\u0001The best way to improve job performance is to leave for work in a good mood. Do your best to fulfill all your Sims' needs before work.",
  "\u0001Maintenance",
  "\u0001Some household items need your care. A wilting violet or murky water in the fish tank are not uncommon. Don't forget to do routine maintenance.",
  "\u0001Mood",
  "\u0001Sims who are in a bad mood are likely to have negative social interactions. Also, they are likely to receive negative reactions if the Sims they're interacting with are in a bad mood.",
  "\u0001Neighbors",
  "\u0001Neighbors from the other houses in the neighborhood will drop by periodically. You can't control neighbors' actions directly but if your Sim is a good host they may become friends.",
  "\u0001Performance",
  "\u0001The game may run faster on your machine if you turn off some of the options. Click the Options button and then the Graphics Options button to see your choices. Click on the icons to see the pop-ups that explain what each option is.",
  "\u0001Personality",
  "\u0001Sims' personalities determine the kind of interactions they like to have. Consult the astrological signs for some clues about which Sims will get along and which will clash.",
  "\u0001Phone",
  "\u0001A phone allows Sims to call acquaintances and order services. They can only call people they've already met, so be sure to greet neighbors when they drop by.",
  "\u0001Plants",
  "\u0001Plants improve the room score. But if they're not cared for, they will die. If your Sims don't have time to care for the plants, be prepared to spend money on a gardener.",
  "\u0001Plants - Move",
  "\u0001To move and delete plants, use the hand tool.",
  "\u0001Room Score",
  "\u0001Sims like big rooms with lots of light; windows help during the day and lamps are good at night. Decorations and landscaping bring this score up, but broken items, dirty dishes, or trash bring things down.",
  "\u0001Routing",
  "\u0001Sims let you know if something is preventing them from getting around. Usually when they stop an action and display an item in their thought bubble, it means that the item is in their way. Switch to Buy Mode and move things around to help them navigate better.",
  "\u0001Save",
  "\u0001In The Sims, the houses are the saved games. Whenever you Quit or return to the Neighborhood screen the changes to the house and its inhabitants can be saved. If you decide you don't like the events that occurred while playing, choose not to save and reenter the house from the Neighborhood screen.",
  "\u0001Skills",
  "\u0001A line under a skill denotes that you need to develop more of this skill before getting a promotion. If so, a line will indicate how many more skill points are needed. Click the skill name to find out how to improve it.",
  "\u0001Social",
  "\u0001Sims are social creatures, and they crave social interactions. They can fulfill their social need by interacting with family, friends, and neighbors. The phone is great for inviting people over.",
  "\u0001Space Bar",
  "\u0001Change the active character by pressing the space bar to cycle through family members (even while a pie menu is up). Or just right-click on the character you'd like to select. Visitors cannot be selected.",
  "\u0001Stairs",
  "\u0001Stairs connect the first story to the second. In order for them to be placed, there has to be open area on both floors. They can also be used outside to connect to balconies, just make sure they can connect to a floor tile on the second story.",
  "\u0001Trees - Shrubs",
  "\u0001Trees and shrubs require no maintenance, so they're a good way to boost outside room score if you can afford the cost and the space.",
  "\u0001Wallpaper",
  "\u0001You can paint or wallpaper a whole room by holding down the Shift key. Click while holding the Shift key if you like it, or release the Shift key if you decide against it.",
  "\u0001Wallpaper - Delete",
  "\u0001To remove paint or wallpaper, hold down the CTRL key while using the Wallpaper Tool. To clear a whole room, hold down both the CTRL and Shift keys while clicking the mouse.\r\n\r\nTIP: Remove paint and wallpaper from a room before repainting it; that way, you'll get some of your original money back. ",
  "\u0001Walls - Delete",
  "\u0001Delete a wall by holding down the CTRL key. The wall cursor will change to a wrecking ball, and drawing over an existing wall will remove it. Keep the CTRL key down until you've released the mouse button.",
  "\u0001Walls - Diagonal",
  "\u0001Diagonal walls can make the house look a little nicer, but you cannot place doors, windows, or objects on them.",
  "\u0001Walls - Room",
  "\u0001Build a complete room by holding the Shift key down while dragging out a wall. Keep the shift key pressed until you release the mouse button.",
  "\u0001Windows",
  "\u0001Sims like rooms with lots of light. The bigger the room, the more windows will be needed to brighten it during the day.",
  "\u0001Windows - Delete",
  "\u0001To delete windows, select the Window Tool and hold down the CTRL key. When the window you'd like to delete is highlighted, click to remove it.\r\n \r\nTIP: You can also remove windows by drawing a wall over them.",
  "\u0003Barre d'espacement",
  "\u0003Changez le personnage actif en appuyant sur la barre d'espacement pour faire d�filer les membres de la famille (m�me si le menu Activit�s est ouvert). Vous pouvez aussi faire un clic-droit sur le personnage. Les visiteurs ne peuvent pas �tre s�lectionn�s.",
  "\u0003T�l�phone",
  "\u0003Avec le t�l�phone, les Sims peuvent contacter leurs amis et obtenir des services. Ils ne peuvent t�l�phoner qu'� des personnes qu'ils ont d�j� rencontr�es, alors dites bonjour � vos voisins quand ils viennent vous voir.",
  "\u0003Performance",
  "\u0003Le jeu peut �tre plus rapide sur votre ordinateur si vous d�sactivez certaines options. Cliquez sur le bouton Options, puis sur Options Graphiques pour faire votre choix. Cliquez sur les ic�nes pour voir appara�tre les explications sur chaque option.",
  "\u0003Voisins",
  "\u0003Les voisins du quartier feront r�guli�rement un petit saut chez vous. Vous ne pouvez pas contr�ler directement leurs faits et gestes, mais si votre Sim les re�oit bien, ils pourront devenir amis.",
  "\u0003Personnalit�",
  "\u0003Les interactions entre Sims d�pendent de leur personnalit�. Etudiez les signes astrologiques pour avoir quelques indices sur les Sims qui s'entendront bien et sur ceux qui ne s'entendront pas.",
  "\u0003Humeur",
  "\u0003Les Sims mal lun�s risquent d'avoir des comportements n�gatifs et de recevoir en retour des r�actions n�gatives d'autres Sims qui sont aussi de mauvaise humeur.",
  "\u0003Int�r�ts",
  "\u0003Les Sims ont des personnalit�s et des int�r�ts vari�s. Ceux d'entre eux qui ont les m�mes go�ts auront des conversations gratifiantes.",
  "\u0003Photo automatique",
  "\u0003Les �v�nements importants de la vie de vos Sims sont automatiquement photographi�s et mis dans l'album photo. Cliquez sur le bouton Album photo dans le mode Cam�ra pour voir les photos.",
  "\u0003Factures",
  "\u0003N'oubliez pas de regarder dans la bo�te aux lettres, les factures arrivent tous les trois jours. Plus vous poss�dez d'objets, plus vous avez de dettes. Payez vos dettes avant que l'huissier ne vienne vous rendre visite. ",
  "\u0003Performance professionnelle",
  "\u0003Le meilleur moyen d'am�liorer ses performances professionnelles est de partir au travail de bonne humeur. Faites de votre mieux pour subvenir � tous les besoins de vos Sims.",
  "\u0003Rotation",
  "\u0003Pour faire pivoter un objet, cliquez dessus et, tout en maintenant le bouton, faites-le glisser dans la direction d�sir�e. Vous pouvez aussi utiliser la touche < & > en tenant l'objet avec la Main, pour faire la m�me op�ration.",
  "\u0003Suppression",
  "\u0003Pour supprimer un objet, s�lectionnez-le puis l�chez le bouton de la souris, ou glissez-le dans le Panneau de contr�le ou appuyez sur Suppr. Si aucun temps Sim ne s'est �coul�, vous r�cup�rez votre argent. Lorsque vous poss�dez un objet depuis un certain temps, sa valeur diminue, mais d'autres objets peuvent voir leur valeur augmenter. On ne vous dira pas lesquels, ce serait de la triche.",
  "\u0003Annulation",
  "\u0003Cliquez sur l'ic�ne Annuler le dernier si vous avez chang� d'avis - continuez � cliquer pour annuler les modifications pr�c�dentes. Vous pourrez r�cup�rer votre argent pour les actions annul�es. Si vous quittez le mode Construction, vos changements seront d�finitifs, vous pourrez les annuler mais vous perdrez de l'argent.",
  "\u0003Vente",
  "\u0003S'il est trop tard pour Annuler le dernier, vous pouvez r�cup�rer l'argent de la plupart des objets de construction en les vendant ou en les annulant. Les objets qu'on peut ramasser peuvent �tre annul�s avec la Main. D'autres outils de construction ont des instructions propres. Cliquez sur l'une des s�lections sous chaque outil pour apprendre comment faire.",
  "\u0003Herbe",
  "\u0003L'herbe poussera d'elle m�me tout le temps.",
  "\u0003Collines",
  "\u0003Maintenez la touche CTRL pour sur�lever le sol et cr�er de jolies collines.",
  "\u0003Plantes",
  "\u0003Les plantes vertes embellissent toutes les pi�ces, mais si personne ne s'en occupe, elles mourront. Si vos Sims n'ont pas le temps de s'en occuper, attendez-vous � payer un jardinier.",
  "\u0003D�placer les plantes",
